  "id": "Compound::DB00495 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Zidovudine is shown to bind to Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including limonene. This binding is supported by multiple paths, each indicating that Cyp2c9 participates in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, a key enzyme in the oxidation of limonene. The shared pathway suggests that Zidovudine may inhibit the activity of Cyp2c19 through a mechanism involving the enzyme Cyp2c9. The evidence from these paths indicates that Zidovudine may act as a substrate or inhibitor of Cyp2c19, potentially affecting the metabolism of limonene and other compounds that are substrates of this enzyme. The consistent interaction between Zidovudine and Cyp2c9 across different paths supports a mechanistic link between the two entities, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
